course: dictionary
lesson: 12785
title: Efficiently: doing a job well
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: When something is done efficiently, it gets the job done well and does not waste time, energy, money or materials. «The team packed the boxes efficiently and finished before lunch.» They did not rush about in a mess or do the job twice, so nothing was wasted.
explain: Efficiently is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. It has more efficiently and most efficiently too. «Maya added the numbers efficiently by using the column method.» The column method is a quick way to add, so she did not waste time counting every single one.
explain: In science, efficiently often means using energy well. «The LED bulb turns electricity into light efficiently.» Very little of the energy is wasted as heat. Ask yourself: did it get the job done without waste? If yes, the word efficiently fits.
fact: Efficiently means in a way that gets a job done well without wasting time, energy, money or materials.
fact: «Work efficiently» means work in a quick, sensible way that avoids mess and wasted effort.
fact: «Use energy efficiently» means use energy well, so less of it is wasted.
fact: «Run efficiently» means work well and without wasting resources, like a machine that uses little power.
fact: Efficiently is related to efficient (adjective) and efficiency (noun): an efficient method saves time, and efficiency is how well you use what you have.
exercise: «The LED bulb turns electricity into light efficiently.» What does efficiently mean here? | Only at night | Slowly, with lots of breaks | Very brightly and loudly | *Using energy well, without wasting it
exercise: «Maya added the numbers efficiently by using the column method.» What does this tell you about Maya? | She counted every single number one by one | *She used a quick method that saved time | She added them with her eyes closed | She gave up on the sum
exercise: «The team packed the boxes efficiently and finished before lunch.» Find and copy the word that tells you how the boxes were packed. | boxes | lunch | *efficiently | packed
test: «The factory runs efficiently, so very little material is thrown away.» What does efficiently suggest? | *It wastes very little | It stops working at lunch | It wastes a lot of materials | It runs very slowly
test: Which sentence shows someone working efficiently? | Ben forgets his pencil and waits for a new one | *Ayla sorts the books by author so she can find each one quickly | Chloe reads the same line ten times | Ahmed spends an hour on a five-minute job
exam: Dev says efficiently means very fast. Is he completely right? | Yes, it means exactly fast and nothing else | Yes, it means slowly | No, it means loudly | *Not quite: it means doing a job well without waste, which can include being quick
